<title>UK: Brazil winter seen slightly cooler this year.</title>
<headline>Brazil winter seen slightly cooler this year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil is likely to have a slightly cooler, drier and windier winter than normal this year and a freeze is possible for coffee areas in late July, a U.S. weather analyst said.</p>
<p>The coldest period is likely to be in late July and most of August, Larry Acker, an analyst at Polo, Il-based 3F (Futures, Farming, Finance) Forecasts, said in his May newsletter.</p>
<p>The timing is not the best for tropical trees and plants, and a freeze is possible (40 percent) for the coffee areas in late July, Acker said.</p>
<p>The period between July 26 and August 4 should see unstable weather and it would be probably the wettest period of the season. It would also be a little cooler than normal, and &quot;frost is possible if the storm patterns allow it,&quot; he added. --Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
